Title:
System Prompts Leaks

Type:
GitHub Tool

Short Summary (4-8 sentences max):
This repository curates “verbatim” system prompts and related instruction layers for many popular LLM products (e.g., OpenAI ChatGPT/Codex, Anthropic Claude/Claude Code, Google Gemini, xAI Grok, Microsoft Copilot, Perplexity, Cursor, and others). It aims to document hidden behavioral rules, tool/agent instructions, skills/commands, and injected reminders that shape model outputs beyond user prompts. The collection is organized by vendor/product and includes variants for web/desktop/mobile, agent modes, tool prompts, and older/deprecated prompt versions. For offensive security, it helps analyze prompt-injection surfaces, tool-call constraints, data exfiltration risks, and guardrail bypass patterns by revealing the exact instruction hierarchy. For defenders and AI product teams, it supports threat modeling, red teaming, and regression testing of policy/guardrail changes over time. It’s interesting because it provides a large comparative dataset of real-world system prompt engineering and agent/tool orchestration patterns across vendors.

Technical Focus:
- System prompt disclosure and instruction hierarchy analysis
- Prompt injection / jailbreak threat modeling
- Agent/tool orchestration prompts (skills, commands, subagents)
- Policy/guardrail and safety instruction patterns
- Versioning/diffing of prompt changes across model releases
- Product-specific injected reminders and API-injected prompts

Use Cases:
- Build prompt-injection test cases tailored to specific assistants/products
- Compare guardrail strategies across vendors and track changes over time
- Identify tool-call and agent workflow constraints to target in red-team exercises
- Create detection rules for suspicious “system prompt extraction” attempts in logs
- Audit AI assistant deployments for unintended instruction leakage or over-privileged tools

Keywords:
system prompt, prompt leakage, prompt injection, jailbreak, LLM guardrails, instruction hierarchy, agentic workflows, tool calling, skills prompts, subagents, API-injected prompts, Claude Code, ChatGPT, Codex, Gemini, Grok, Copilot, Perplexity, Cursor, safety policies